<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    {{ icon("work-visas", 56) }}
    <p class="tag">Core Service</p>
    <h1>Work &amp; Employment Visas</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">The right work authorisation for your role, without guessing which permit applies.</p>

    <p>Foreign nationals taking up pre-arranged employment in the Philippines may require a 9(g) Pre-Arranged Employment Visa, together with other applicable employment and immigration authorisations depending on the circumstances. Foreign Immigration Services assists employees and employers in identifying the appropriate pathway, preparing the required documentation and coordinating the immigration process.</p>

    <div class="media-split">
      <div>
        <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Assessing whether your role calls for a long-term work visa, a short-term work permit, or a bridging arrangement while a longer-term application is processed</li>
          <li>Assisting with 9(g) Pre-Arranged Employment Visa applications and related immigration processing</li>
          <li>Coordinating with the Department of Labor and Employment where an employment permit is a prerequisite to your visa</li>
          <li>Preparing and organising the required documentation</li>
          <li>Keeping you and your employer informed as the application progresses</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="media-split__media">
        {{ mediaPanel("work-visas", "wide") }}
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Taking up a long-term role with a Philippine employer</li>
      <li>A short-term or project-based assignment</li>
      <li>Starting work while a longer-term application is still being processed</li>
      <li>Other employment-related immigration circumstances</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us about the role and the assignment.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We review your circumstances and identify the pathway that applies.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We help prepare and organise the required documentation, coordinating with your employer where needed.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>We submit your application and monitor its progress.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What We May Need From You</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your passport and current immigration status</li>
      <li>Details of your employer, role and the expected duration of the assignment</li>
      <li>Employer-provided documentation such as an employment contract or assignment letter, where applicable</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Starting a Role in the Philippines?</h2>
      <p>Tell us about your assignment and we will identify the right pathway.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=work-visas">Request a Work Visa Assessment</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Can I start working before my long-term visa is approved?</summary>
        <p>In some circumstances a bridging arrangement may allow work to begin while a longer-term application is still pending. Tell us about your timeline and we'll advise whether this applies to your situation.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is this only for individual employees, or can employers use this too?</summary>
        <p>Both. If your organisation is hiring or relocating more than one employee, see also <a href="/services/corporate-and-global-mobility/">Corporate &amp; Global Mobility</a>.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

